WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 24 - Beautiful Maze

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.370
Rei!

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.270
Are you Maya Kitajima?!

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.590
Can we have your autograph?

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.180
Wow, Maya's a real star!

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.580
It's Mr. Masumi!

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.650
You're a hit, little one.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.840
I'm so happy to see you again!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.160
Little one, your Helen has proved quite popular.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.600
Ticket sales are going well, too.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.720
Yes! Thank you very much, Mr. Hayami!

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.800
I hope you'll be able to maintain that energy until the final show.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:26.640
I wonder when you're finally going to stop making that face at me.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.950
Well, what am I supposed to do?

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.970
The Daito Demon told me to watch what I say!

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.310
Mr. Hayami told you that?

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.280
Yeah.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.810
Which is why I took the trouble to greet him properly.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:41.980
I didn't think it'd make him burst out laughing!

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.940
Mr. Hayami might actually be a nice guy.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.920
Are you kidding me? That workaholic?

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.940
Well, this is one business where you can't afford to make enemies.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.360
I think he's been trying to teach you that much.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.930
Teach me? Him?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.940
A purple rose?

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.870
He's here. He's somewhere in the crowd.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.550
Mr. Purple Roses!

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.300
Excuse me, but did you catch sight of the man that threw this purple rose?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.260
Hm...

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.230
Look, it's the girl who plays Helen!

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.610
You're right!

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.630
I want her autograph.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.260
Are you Miss Maya Kitajima?

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.940
Can I shake your hand?

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.170
Could I have your autograph?

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:42.230
Excuse me, let me through. I'm looking for someone at the moment and...

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.100
Are you all right?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.020
I'm fine. Thank you.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.800
Why is he helping me?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.960
Glad to hear that.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:12.550
I wouldn't want anything to happen to our valuable commodity.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.140
Take it from me: I'll make sure I don't get sick...

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.580
nor be involved in an accident until the play has finished its run!

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.730
Very well.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.650
For Ayumi, <i>The Miracle Worker</i> ends a day before Maya's involvement.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.350
Though critics have hailed her performance as her highest achievement to date,

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:40.270
Ayumi cannot feel completely content with their praise.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.120
<i>The Miracle Worker</i>

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.520
I played the best Helen I could.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.650
There were no flaws in my acting.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.470
And yet, my mother hasn't kissed me once.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:58.730
Why? Maya Kitajima, what do you have that I don't?

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.690
The lead role? Me?

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.970
We'd like you to play the lead role in our play first of all.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:16.160
Then, later, we'd like to move you into television or movies.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.930
Do you really mean it?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.420
Masumi Hayami!

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.770
This is bad news!

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.480
You can't let yourself be swayed by these smooth-talkers.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.180
Those guys are nothing but scouts for disreputable agencies.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:49.250
They weren't offering anything decent. Don't lower your standards!

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:51.560
How is it even your business?

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.900
Please leave me alone!

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.140
Little one...

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.930
You are currently nominated for this year's Best Supporting Actress Award...

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.980
at the Theater Festival.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.130
I am?

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.280
Winners of the award have a shot at appearing on a serial drama on MBA TV...

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.650
and are offered a lot more roles.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.860
You happen to be the favorite this year.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:19.270
I am? Really?

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.970
Sure. Yes, I'll come to the award ceremony.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:27.230
Thank you.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:34.210
Miss, have you just been nominated for the Best Supporting Actress Award at the Theater Festival?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.720
Yes. My mother's practically a shoe-in for the Best Actress Award.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.530
Well, that's just... Miss?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:45.210
They told me Maya Kitajima has also been nominated for the Best Supporting Actress Award.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:50.970
Oh, but I'm sure the judges will choose you over her.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.420
Can you please make me some tea?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.630
I want to be alone with my thoughts.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.240
Miss...

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:12.470
And the two remaining contenders from the five nominees for the award...

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:17.330
of Best Supporting Actress are: Ayumi Himekawa, from <i>The Miracle Worker</i>,

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:22.360
and Maya Kitajima, from the same play.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.010
And now, I will announce the winner of the Best Supporting Actress Award.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:31.930
It goes to:

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.270
Maya Kitajima!

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.710
Maya, it's you!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.720
Miss Maya Kitajima, please come to the stage.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.210
You need to go up on stage!

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.230
Go.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:10.260
Miss Maya Kitajima, your portrayal of Helen Keller combined a fresh dimension...

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.100
with beautiful acting. It impressed us immensely.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.550
I hereby present you with the award for Best Supporting Actress.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.760
Can we have a few words from you, Miss Kitajima?

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:33.010
Well, you see, I've never received an award before, and my grades in school...

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:38.770
were never that good, so this is like a dream come true and... ouch!

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.260
The role of Best Actress was awarded to Utako Himekawa for her portrayal...

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:44.760
of Annie Sullivan.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:50.290
It's pretty cruel to sit and watch awards being picked up by your rival and your mother.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:54.310
This is probably the prodigy's first defeat.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.770
Congratulations, Mom.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.270
Thank you, Ayumi.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:10.070
Congratulations on winning the Best Supporting Actress Award, Maya Kitajima.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.520
Thank you, Ayumi!

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.770
However, I don't consider myself defeated.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:16.690
What?

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:22.590
Your "fresh" portrayal of Helen may have stolen the show because of your own personal charm,

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.930
but I was the one who played Helen perfectly.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:31.240
Hearing the critics today made me realize the differences between your Helen and mine.

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:32.930
Ayumi?

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:37.690
It renewed my confidence that I played the perfect Helen.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.260
It's Chigusa Tsukikage.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.560
From <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.260
She used to be a superstar.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.610
Ms. Tsukikage...

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.340
Can I please come up on stage?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:54.930
By all means.

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:57.810
We have a very special guest here tonight.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:02.180
Once the star of the fabled phantom masterpiece of the theatrical world, <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>,

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:07.890
she has coached Utako Himekawa and Maya Kitajima - Ms. Chigusa Tsukikage!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:14.720
So what's your opinion of the two Helens, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.920
Both Helens had rare potential.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:23.010
And both of these actresses are worthy of playing the Scarlet Angel.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.680
Maya, do you want to play the Scarlet Angel?

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:32.840
Me? Playing the Scarlet Angel?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.550
That's what I asked.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.270
Masumi!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.040
Oh no!

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:42.870
So many actresses have coveted the role.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.050
I can't even move!

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:48.040
Well, what do you say, Maya?

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.290
I'll do it,

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:55.550
Ms. Tsukikage. I'll do my very best!

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:02.980
Ayumi, do you wish to play the Scarlet Angel as well?

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.390
Alongside Maya?

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.500
I would love to, Ms. Tsukikage!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:13.520
She's letting Ayumi and Maya play the role I've sought for so long?

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:21.300
Before you discovered these two, you'd all but sealed off the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.780
And now, I'd like to announce to everyone present here tonight...

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:30.130
that these two actresses will be playing the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:33.220
Maya Kitajima and Ayumi Himekawa!

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:35.300
This is huge!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.230
Their rivalry has only just begun.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:42.060
I will be watching to see how they grow and improve as actresses...

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:45.990
before making my final decision as to which one of them will take the role...

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.520
of the Scarlet Angel.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.260
You've beaten me again, Ms. Tsukikage.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:02.250
I'm not giving up the rights to <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>, even if I die.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:06.590
You can go ahead and tell your father that as well.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:13.560
Maya, it all starts right here.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.050
We'll see how far your acting will take you.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.700
May I have this dance?

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.990
I can't dance.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.020
Don't worry, I'm not going to do anything embarrassing.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.500
But I...

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:42.190
Put your hand here.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.220
You've got it.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.930
You're not half bad.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.890
Everyone's staring at us.

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.980
Let them. It's good publicity.

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:13.970
It's like... that day last summer...

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.650
But it couldn't possibly be him!

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.740
It's a bit too early for a love scene, don't you think, little one?

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:32.110
You just raised her market price.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.630
Take a look.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.620
Your little plan seems to have worked.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.750
But I'd be careful if I were you.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.560
There are thousands of demons watching you,

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.820
ready to expose your weakness.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.760
What do you mean by that?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.130
Nothing. I was merely speculating whether...

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.780
your heart's latent kindness might have finally awoken.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:49.890
What kindness?

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:55.470
Why don't you just send her some more purple roses and encourage her a little more?

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:07.520
And now, we will announce our casting decisions for MBA's upcoming...

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:09.030
serial drama.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:14.270
It's an ambitious piece with an A-list cast about the Westernization of Japan.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.710
"I don't believe a word of it."

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.380
Can you try that one more time?

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:21.770
Yes.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.260
"I don't believe a word of it."

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.520
Again.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:33.010
"I don't believe a word of it."

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:38.510
It's like you were a different person every time you said it.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:42.610
Well, I haven't grasped Satoko just yet,

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.280
so I don't know how I should act out this line.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.740
So young and already she's getting cocky.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.860
Just do what comes naturally.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.230
Okay.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:56.430
What does he mean by that?

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:02.000
Hang on.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.010
Have you done any Japanese traditional dance before?

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.420
Only a tiny bit.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.060
You don't have a good stance.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.480
Your body is too stiff.

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:13.540
I want you to rectify that before we start filming!

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.730
I apologize for interrupting your work, Mr. Masumi.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:34.640
You have a visitor.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:37.930
I thought I told you not to let anyone in for the time being.

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.870
But...

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:47.420
Well, to what do I owe the pleasure of this visit?

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.080
Welcome back!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.780
Get your things together. You're moving out of this place.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:58.720
What?

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:01.470
You're moving in to the Daito Theater.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:04.060
We've arranged a dorm room for you there.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.580
The Daito Theater?!

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.300
But Ms. Tsukikage would never allow it!

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.300
Actually, she was the one who asked for the arrangement.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.510
That's a lie! I don't believe you!

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:19.600
You really don't seem to understand how much trouble you cause her.

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:22.660
You don't think it's troublesome for her to live in this tiny hole with you,

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.430
having to deal with your homework and your rehearsals,

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.250
when she's as physically weak as she is?

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:32.270
Ms. Tsukikage will be able to become an acting coach again.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:36.260
Isn't it nice that the Daito Theater can help her?

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:44.800
So, she traded me for the opportunity to teach acting again?

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.530
From now on, you'll be living here and you won't have a single worry...

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.180
to distract you from your acting.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:59.670
Was I really a nuisance, ma'am?

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:01.180
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:07.340
Until you find yourself a proper manager, I'll be looking after you.

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.360
They just want you to keep an eye on me. That's it, isn't it?

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.470
After your third lesson you will leave school early for rehearsals.

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:16.840
Then, after lunch, you have a costume fitting at the MBA.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.550
Then, you've got a poster shoot at two.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.090
At three, you have your Japanese traditional dance lesson.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.890
Japanese traditional dance lesson?!

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.890
Hey, that's her!

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:36.210
She looks a bit pathetic, though.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:39.260
Can she really pull off being a nobleman's daughter?

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:52.560
Wow, it looks just like the real thing.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:56.380
Is this where I'll become Satoko?

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.770
Satoko Tanuma.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:03.800
She was the only girl who sailed to the West in the black ships...

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:06.660
and actually lived there in <i>Civilization and Enlightenment.</i>

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:09.660
I'll do it!

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:12.830
I may not be much and I may be useless at everything else,

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:15.170
but here, I can become the daughter of a nobleman!

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:18.450
I'll do it!

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.230
Episode 1, Scene 42.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.490
Now, in Scene 45, we're in the living room of the Tanuma family.

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:32.900
Father, won't you show me those black ships too?

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:37.090
No, no, you have to be more adorable there!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.710
If you try to convince him the same way you use the spear,

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:42.090
your father's never going to listen to you!

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.360
Yes, sir.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.550
It's a lot different from the stage, isn't it?

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:50.600
Television depends on minute-to-minute, second-splitting acting.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:51.550
I see.

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:54.380
I haven't been able to switch between moods as quick as I need to.

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:57.880
This is the world of TV. It's very different from the world of acting.

00:18:57.880 --> 00:19:01.120
I wonder if I can do it.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:06.150
I don't want to. There's no way you're going to make me sign this!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:11.140
I'm not going to sign until you let me see Ms. Tsukikage...

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:15.820
and I hear from her own mouth the reasons for putting me in the Daito Theater.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:30.410
This is a special acting school that hones the acting skills of professionals.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:34.430
This is not part of Daito Entertainment; my father runs it separately as a side project.

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:37.440
More to the right. To the right!

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.010
Stop there.

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.000
Ma'am!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.890
Mr. Masumi, I'll have to ask you to take care of this girl...

00:19:46.890 --> 00:19:49.980
because I've washed my hands of her for now.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:55.760
Why have you done this? Why have you put me in the care of Daito Entertainment?

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:58.000
I wanted to stay with you and the others!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.490
Don't be so naive, Maya.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:03.620
Everyone is always alone.

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:07.180
What do you think your rival for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i> is doing at this very moment?

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:09.180
Ma'am...

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:12.160
Maya Kitajima

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:15.320
I'd like to say goodbye to Rei and the others.

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:16.340
May I?

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:19.550
Yes, but you won't be allowed to see them after this.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:23.260
Your friends may offer you momentary comfort, but beyond that,

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:26.020
they won't be of any use to you.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.190
How can you say that?

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.500
You're going to become a star.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:32.180
From now on, you must choose your friends based on how useful they'll be.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:36.250
I have a package for you.

00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:39.160
Purple roses?

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:42.230
I'm sure he'd also be very happy...

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:45.780
if you become a star.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.180
What were you trying to do?

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.750
Excuse me?

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.180
I'm talking about the purple roses.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.800
The only person who knows that...

00:20:57.800 --> 00:21:01.180
would be the real sender of the purple roses.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:04.660
Which means the cat's out of the bag.

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:08.840
It's funny how much you, who hides his heart from human eyes...

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.480
It's funny how much you love that girl.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.190
What are you talking about?

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:20.480
I know how much you care for her.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:24.320
You're in love with her!

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:26.220
That's preposterous! A little girl like that?!

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:28.420
And what does that have to do with anything?

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.040
That's the excuse you've used this entire time...

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.730
to deny your own feelings!

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.680
Have I hit the nail on the head?

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:37.690
That's enough!

00:21:39.220 --> 00:21:41.840
She's growing up fast.

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:44.220
Soon, she'll be old enough for you to make love to her.

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:48.800
Me? In love with someone?

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
Asa kara yoru made yoru kara asa made

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:15.370
From morning until night, from dusk till dawn,

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
Futari ai no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:15.910 --> 00:22:23.310
you can feel the warmth of our love.

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
Shunkashuutou mo ippun ichibyou mo

00:22:23.310 --> 00:22:30.000
All year round, every minute and every second,

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
Futari hada no ondo wo itsumo kanjiru desho

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.940
you can feel the warmth of our skin.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
Kono dokidoki wa makka ni moeru taiyou

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:46.190
This excitement is burning brightly like the sun,

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
Atsuku moete atsuku togashite

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.480
let us burn brightly, let us burn until we're hot

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
Koi wo shimashou!

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.290
and make love!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.990
It's so Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:00.760
Make it Make it Naked!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Let's hold and be true to each other!

00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:04.070
Sunao na mama dakiaou!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
And let's add more heat! I love the heat!

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:10.570
Isso mekimeki nekki! mekimeki daisuki!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Feel the love!

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:13.960
Aishiae!

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:25.260
I can't believe I'm actually in a TV show!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:27.590
I haven't quite gotten the hang of TV acting though,

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:29.560
but I have to try my hardest to get Satoko down.

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.230
I hear that Ayumi's going to be in a show too.

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.350
But I'm a bit lonely and I'm worried about Ms. Tsukikage,

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:39.450
my mother and the others.

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:42.320
That's when Satomi gives me courage.

00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:45.940
I can't seem to forget your smile.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 25 - Heavenly Light

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:50.620
This is strange! I've never felt like this before!
